{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation, etc., on the first of the month.</b> The verse informs us that on the very day itself the Jews assembled for the matter, and this fact tells that each person had his lineage ready at hand without the trouble of proof and testimony. Also, on that very day the lineages of all of them were recognized, and this is the verse's saying <b>and they declared their pedigrees</b> immediately after the statement ״on the first of the month״ etc.:" "<b>And they declared their pedigrees, etc.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, wrote: they brought the book of their lineages and witnesses to the established record of each one's birth, to trace his descent to the tribe. And Ramban objected, for they had no need for any of this — thus far. Perhaps it is because they needed an established record of birth to exclude a mamzer who recognizes his father, for the determination of his mamzerut would be from the birth, and it is necessary to bring an established record of birth — meaning that he was born in validity; and otherwise, the mamzer could cite a book of lineages going back to Jacob, which his mother declared to him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The verb וַיִּתְיַלְדוּ is rendered 'and they declared their pedigrees' following Rashi's interpretation cited in comment 1."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:52.419950356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}